		{/* ART ------------------------------------------------------------ */}
		<section class="ds-demo__section" id="art">
			<Heading as="h2" size={2} variant="secondary" class="ds-demo__h">Art — tokens and the frame</Heading>
			<p class="ds-demo__note">
				The illustration language the plates are drawn in (tokens.overrides.css →
				ART; <code>ArtFrame</code>; art-frame.css): white 1px line work and flat fills
				in four colours on a near-black landscape plate. The plate follows the
				theme: on the cream page it is the first wash (<code>--wash-1</code>) and the
				ink is the secondary ink, so the same drawing reads as ink on paper, with the
				white faces dark and the fills a step deeper; at night it is the card. A file names no colour but these tokens, and the frame owns the
				plate, the edge, the corner, the line weights and the motion, so the whole
				language retunes in one place. Every file starts from <code>packages/design-system/src/art/_template.svg</code>.
			</p>
			<div class="ds-demo__swatches">
				{artTokens.map(([name, note]) => (
					<div class="ds-demo__swatch-row">
						{name === "--art-plate" || name === "--art-edge" ? (
							<span class="ds-demo__swatch" style={`background: var(${name}); border-color: var(--art-edge)`} />
						) : name === "--art-radius" ? (
							<span class="ds-demo__swatch" style="background: var(--art-plate); border-color: var(--art-edge); border-radius: var(--art-radius)" />
						) : name === "--duration-loop" ? (
							<span class="ds-demo__swatch" style="border-style: dashed" />
						) : (
							<span class="ds-demo__swatch ds-demo__swatch--art" style={`--swatch: var(${name})`}><i /></span>
						)}
						<Mono variant="value">{name}</Mono>
						<Mono variant="text">{note}</Mono>
					</div>
				))}
			</div>

			<h2 class="ds-demo__h ds-demo__h--sub">The frame — the template at tile size and hero size</h2>
			<p class="ds-demo__note">
				<code>&lt;ArtFrame svg={"{raw}"} label="…" /&gt;</code> inlines the file on the
				plate (<code>role="img"</code>); with no label, or <code>decorative</code>, it is
				aria-hidden and the link around it names it. The box is the file's 16:9
				and clips (<code>--art-ratio</code> retunes it in scope). Strokes are <code>vector-effect="non-scaling-stroke"</code>, so the line is 1px at 230px
				and at 720px alike.
			</p>
			<div class="ds-demo__art-sizes">
				<ArtFrame svg={artTemplate} label="_template.svg at tile size" />
				<ArtFrame svg={artTemplate} label="_template.svg at hero size" />
			</div>

			<h2 class="ds-demo__h ds-demo__h--sub">Both themes — the plate follows the page</h2>
			<p class="ds-demo__note">
				The same file on each theme's page (<code>ThemePage</code>): the warm dark
				plate and white line on the dark page, the pale wash and the dark ink on cream.
			</p>
			<div class="ds-demo__art-themes">
				{(["light", "dark"] as const).map((t) => (
					<ThemePage theme={t}>
						<ArtFrame svg={artTemplate} label={`_template.svg on the ${t} theme`} />
					</ThemePage>
				))}
			</div>

			<h2 class="ds-demo__h ds-demo__h--sub">Line weights</h2>
			<p class="ds-demo__note">
				Top to bottom: <code>.art-line</code> (1, the inherited default), <code>.art-line--2</code> (1.5, one emphasis outline), <code>--art-ink-2</code> for the secondary line, and the two dash patterns, <code>4 4</code> and <code>2 6</code>.
			</p>
			<div class="ds-demo__art-sizes">
				<ArtFrame svg={artLines} label="the two line weights and two dash patterns, at tile size" />
				<ArtFrame svg={artLines} label="the two line weights and two dash patterns, at hero size" />
			</div>

			<h2 class="ds-demo__h ds-demo__h--sub">Motion — five kinds, paused until hovered</h2>
			<p class="ds-demo__note">
				A file marks one group <code>data-motion</code> and the frame owns the
				keyframes, timed by <code>--duration-loop</code> (<code>data-speed</code> 0.5 / 1 / 2
				divides it). Paused at rest — the still frame is the poster — and running on
				hover, focus, inside a hovered link, or with <code>play</code> (<code>data-art-play</code>). Under reduced motion the loop is 0s and nothing
				moves. The first frame sits inside a link.
			</p>
			<label class="ds-demo__art-toggle">
				<input type="checkbox" data-art-play-toggle />
				<Mono variant="text">play all — sets data-art-play on each frame</Mono>
			</label>
			<div class="ds-demo__art-grid">
