							<Mono variant="text">{note}</Mono>
						</figcaption>
					</figure>
				))}
			</div>

		</section>

		{/* GLYPHS --------------------------------------------------------- */}
		<section class="ds-demo__section" id="glyphs">
			<Heading as="h2" size={2} variant="secondary" class="ds-demo__h">Glyphs — micrographics and the keycap tile</Heading>
			<p class="ds-demo__note">
				The micrographics (<code>packages/design-system/src/glyphs/</code>; <code>Glyph</code>, <code>GlyphTile</code>; glyph.css and motion.css): hairline
				marks on a 48×32 grid, inlined beside text. Their line work is <code>currentColor</code> — the ink of the text they sit in, dimmed through <code>--glyph-dim</code> (that ink at 40%, resolved on the glyph) — and their
				colour is the art palette, so a glyph follows the theme as the art does. A
				glyph is BAKED from a recipe (<code>src/glyphs/recipes/&lt;name&gt;.ts</code>, a
				few lines on the L0 kit; <code>bun run glyphs:bake</code> writes the file under a
				header, <code>glyphs:check</code> fails on a stale one) or hand-drawn; the
				registry (<code>glyphs.ts</code>, <code>GLYPH_NAMES</code>) reads only the files.
				Where <code>Icon</code> is a UI affordance — a 2px stroke in the ink, a meaning —
				a glyph is a mark: decorative or data, hairline, aria-hidden unless it says <code>label</code>.
			</p>
			<p class="ds-demo__note">
				<Anchor href="/design-system/glyphs/" arrow="right">The glyph tile sheet</Anchor> shows every glyph and a spread of every generator in tiles, grouped by family (A waves to I bold shapes), a type &amp; modules specimen, with the L3 signal chain and a readouts panel; one tile is <code>/design-system/glyphs#glyph-&lt;name&gt;</code>.
			</p>

			<h2 class="ds-demo__h ds-demo__h--sub">Inline — in a line of text, and on the size scale</h2>
			<p class="ds-demo__note"> <code>&lt;Glyph name /&gt;</code> in text is 1em tall, as wide as the viewBox
				makes it (3:2), centred on the x-height, in the text's ink. <code>size</code> is its height on the space scale, numbered as <code>Icon</code>'s size is: 6 (32px, the viewBox at 1×), 8, 10 (2×), 12 (3×).
			</p>
			<Body>
				A red <Glyph name="plus" /> beside a word, a signal <Glyph name="ring-in" label="a signal arriving" /> arriving
				(that one has a label, so it is an image), and a <Glyph name="toggle" /> toggle,
				whose pill is the dimmed ink: three glyphs in a reading line.
			</Body>
			<div class="ds-demo__glyph-sizes">
				{([6, 8, 10, 12] as const).map((s) => (
					<figure class="ds-demo__glyph-size">
						<Glyph name="ring-in" size={s} />
						<figcaption><Mono variant="text">size={s}</Mono></figcaption>
					</figure>
				))}
				<figure class="ds-demo__glyph-size" style="color: var(--art-green)">
					<Glyph name="toggle" size={10} />
					<figcaption><Mono variant="text">size={10}, coloured</Mono></figcaption>
				</figure>
			</div>

			<h2 class="ds-demo__h ds-demo__h--sub">Tiles — the keycap, on both pages</h2>
			<p class="ds-demo__note"> <code>&lt;GlyphTile label&gt;</code>: a 3:2 cap in the rim's hairline
				(<code>--art-edge</code>) on a wash, the caps label under it (a prop, or the <code>label</code> slot), and a <code>readout</code> slot drawn over the mark in
				the thin numeral. The tile sizes the glyph and fills its column, so a row of
				them sits on a <code>Grid</code>. Hover a tile and its glyph's motion runs (the
				ring's dash crawls); <code>play</code> on the glyph, or <code>data-art-play</code> on any ancestor, runs it from the start; under reduced motion nothing moves.
			</p>
			<div class="ds-demo__art-themes">
				{(["light", "dark"] as const).map((t) => (
					<ThemePage theme={t}>
						<Grid templateColumns="repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr))" gap={4} data-glyph-tiles={t}>
							<GlyphTile label="plus"><Glyph name="plus" /></GlyphTile>
							<GlyphTile label="ring-in"><Glyph name="ring-in" /></GlyphTile>
							<GlyphTile label="toggle"><Glyph name="toggle" /></GlyphTile>
							<GlyphTile label="readout"><Glyph name="ring-in" /><span slot="readout">34</span></GlyphTile>
							<GlyphTile label="play"><Glyph name="ring-in" play /></GlyphTile>
							<GlyphTile><Mono slot="label" tone="primary">label slot</Mono><Glyph name="toggle" /></GlyphTile>
						</Grid>
					</ThemePage>
				))}
			</div>

			<h2 class="ds-demo__h ds-demo__h--sub">Generators — a mark drawn from props, one per family</h2>
			<p class="ds-demo__note"> A generator (<code>Wave</code>, <code>Envelope</code>, <code>Filter</code>, <code>Curve</code>, <code>Gauge</code>, <code>Dial</code>, <code>Ladder</code>, <code>Segments</code>, <code>Selector</code>, <code>Fan</code>, <code>Rings</code>, <code>Matrix</code>) is a pure function in <code>lib/micro/gen/</code> behind a thin component, rendered through the same host as <code>Glyph</code>: the same size, label, play and ARIA. A labelled <code>Gauge</code>, <code>Dial</code> or <code>Ladder</code> is a <code>role="meter"</code>. Every variant is on the sheet.
			</p>
			<Grid templateColumns="repeat(auto-fill, minmax(calc(var(--space-12) * 1.5), 1fr))" gap={4} data-glyph-generators>
				<GlyphTile label="A · wave"><Wave shape="sine" /></GlyphTile>
				<GlyphTile label="B · filter"><Filter type="bp" q={3} /></GlyphTile>
				<GlyphTile label="C · gauge"><Gauge value={0.62} label="Level" /></GlyphTile>
				<GlyphTile label="D · fan"><Fan /></GlyphTile>
				<GlyphTile label="E · matrix"><Matrix hot={[2, 2]} /></GlyphTile>
			</Grid>
		</section>

		<section class="ds-demo__section" id="readouts">
			<Heading as="h2" size={2} variant="secondary" class="ds-demo__h">Readouts — the text beside a mark</Heading>
			<p class="ds-demo__note">
				The synth panel pairs its marks with small typographic readouts, and they are HTML text, never inside an SVG (family G on the <Anchor href="/design-system/glyphs/#family-G">glyph sheet</Anchor>). Label and thin numeral is <code>Stat variant="numeral"</code>; the boxed and arrow tags are <code>Chip</code>'s <code>tone="accent"</code> and <code>variant="arrow"</code>. The three below are new: each sits centred in a <code>GlyphTile</code>'s cap where a glyph would.
			</p>

			<h2 class="ds-demo__h ds-demo__h--sub">ReadoutStack — values, one emphasised</h2>
			<p class="ds-demo__note">
				<code>&lt;ReadoutStack values active&gt;</code>: a list, the emphasised value <code>aria-current="true"</code> — drawn in the thin numeral (<code>--font-display</code> at <code>--font-size-6</code>), the rest the label voice in the tertiary ink. <code>active</code> is an index, clamped. Name it with <code>aria-label</code>.
			</p>
